This repository contains only its own code: install and uninstall scripts, patch
layers, configuration templates and documentation. The sources and builds of the
projects listed below are NOT redistributed here - the installer fetches them
from their official sources (the npm registry, GitHub) on the user's machine and
applies the patches locally, after installation.

The projects the stand is built on, and their licenses:

  DeepSeek Harness           MIT           https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness
  dsh-better-sidebar         MIT           https://github.com/omdsh-dev/DSH-better-sidebar
  @wenbin_wb/dsh-bridge      MIT           https://github.com/wenbin-wb/dsh-bridge
  @anionex/dsh-turn-rewind   BSD-3-Clause  https://github.com/Anionex/dsh-turn-rewind
  dsh-plugin                 MIT           https://github.com/dshplugin/dsh-plugin-hub
  dsh-univer-office          Apache-2.0    https://github.com/dream-num/dsh-univer-office
  dsh-context                Apache-2.0    https://github.com/bowenliang123/dsh-context
  graph-memory               MIT           https://github.com/adoresever/graph-memory
  llama.cpp                  MIT           https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp

The changes these scripts make to those packages after installation are described
in the README ("Why the patch layers") and in the header of every script: the
file, the anchor and the reason. Not one modified file of those projects is part
of this repository.

The single exception is the bridge UI translation dictionary
(projects/PlugIN/dsh-bridge-en/tools/strings.json, occ.json, tr-*.json). Those are
INTERFACE STRINGS extracted from the sources of @wenbin_wb/dsh-bridge (MIT),
together with their positions in the files and the English translations. Without
them the translation cannot be re-applied after a plugin update, so they are
included under the plugin's own MIT terms: authorship and license are stated
above, and the change (Chinese strings replaced by English) is described in
projects/PlugIN/dsh-bridge-en/README.md. No executable code of the plugin is in
this repository.

The stand's own code is under the MIT license, see LICENSE.

The chat template templates/chat-agent.jinja is derived from the template baked
into the Qwen3 model (Apache-2.0): the same logic with one changed condition that
keeps repeated reasoning out of the history. The condition and the reason are
described in a comment inside the file.
